    <div>
      <span class="eyebrow">About Tatiana</span>
      <h2>Rooted in Colorado, built for recovery</h2>
      <p>As a life-long Coloradan, I am passionate about caring for the body that allows me to play as much as possible. I enjoy skiing, biking, running, and anything that lets me be outdoors. At the same time, yoga taught me that if I treated my body with the same reverence that I treated the outdoors, my mood, balance, and performance was all enhanced.</p>
      <p>From being a collegiate athlete, to trail runner, enduro biker, and outdoor enthusiast, I know first hand the importance of recovery throughout training, and help my clients build a steady relationship with the kinds of self-care that aren't just pampering, but required for performance.</p>
      <p class="pull-quote">I believe that strength — in all aspects of life — comes from understanding.</p>
      <p>I am a Massage Therapist and Yoga Therapist and use that combined knowledge to take a holistic approach to injury, pain, and compensation patterns, working to create change from the inside out. This trauma-informed approach ensures each client's needs are met in a way that feels accessible and appropriate.</p>
      <p>I work to observe &amp; explore the body &amp; mind through touch, breath, meditation, mindfulness, and massage to gain true understanding of myself, my clients, and the world we inhabit.</p>
      <p><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Let's Connect.</a></p>
    </div>
